strant also agrees to:</p>\n                <p>\n                    - Provide full and accurate registration and contact information as required<br>\n                    - Maintain technical and administrative domain control data<br>\n                    - Be bound by the ICANN UDRP for dispute resolution\n                </p>\n                <h3>4. .BIZ Domains (Commercial Use Requirement)</h3>\n                <p>Registrants of .BIZ domains agree that:</p>\n                <p>\n                    - The domain must be used for bona fide business or commercial purposes<br>\n                    - The domain must not be registered solely for resale, leasing, or trading<br>\n                    - The Registrant confirms: The domain is related to a legitimate business purpose; The registration is not speculative or abusive<br>\n                    Disputes may be handled under ICANN policies and .BIZ-specific dispute frameworks (including STOP and RDRP where applicable).\n                </p>\n                <h3>5. .INFO Domains</h3>\n                <p>For .INFO domains, the Registrant agrees to:</p>\n                <p>\n                    - ICANN UDRP dispute resolution<br>\n                    - Registry-specific launch period policies (including Sunrise rules if applicable)<br>\n                    - Acknowledge that the registry operator has no liability for allocation or dispute outcomes during launch periods\n                </p>\n                <h3>6. .NAME Domains (Personal Name Only)</h3>\n                <p>Registrants must ensure:</p>\n                <p>\n                    - The domain represents a personal name (legal name or commonly known name)<br>\n                    - Registration is first-come, first-served unless overridden by dispute decisions<br>\n                    - Compliance with: Eligibility Requirements (ERDRP), UDRP policies, Registry restrictions on name use\n                </p>\n                <p>Additional .NAME Email Forward